 ## Overview
-Hierarchical Grid Traversal is a ray-grid traversal algorithm that iterates through levels of a grid mipmap to efficiently march a ray through sparse volume data [S1, S2, unofficial]. It starts at the root (level 0) and recursively visits child voxels only if the ray intersects the parent voxel's axis-aligned bounding box (AABB), using lookup tables to map parent indices to child indices [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard voxel DDA which checks every voxel, this method leverages the hierarchical tree structure to skip empty space by jumping between grid nodes of different resolutions [S1, S2, unofficial]. It is distinct from [Hierarchical Digital Differential Analyzer (HDDA)](1122-hierarchical-digital-differential-analyzer-hdda.md) in its specific implementation for VDB structures using compile-time template meta-programming, and from [Hierarchical Trilinear Ray Casting](851-hierarchical-trilinear-ray-casting.md) by focusing on traversal efficiency rather than shading interpolation [S1, S5, unofficial].
+Hierarchical Grid Traversal is a ray-grid traversal method that iterates through levels of a grid mipmap, starting at the root and recursively visiting child voxels only if the ray intersects the parent voxel's axis-aligned bounding box (AABB) [S1, S2, unofficial]. It uses lookup tables to map parent voxel indices to child voxel indices, accelerating rendering by skipping empty space at coarse levels [S1, unofficial]. Unlike standard voxel DDA which checks every voxel, this method leverages the hierarchical tree structure to significantly accelerate ray-marching for sparse volumes [S1, S4, unofficial]. It is distinct from [Hierarchical Digital Differential Analyzer (HDDA)](1122-hierarchical-digital-differential-analyzer-hdda.md) in its specific implementation for VDB structures using compile-time template meta-programming, and from [Hierarchical Trilinear Ray Casting](851-hierarchical-trilinear-ray-casting.md) by focusing on traversal efficiency rather than shading interpolation [S1, S5, unofficial].
 
